No, what really makes Gehennom too easy is the fact that if you don't
overprepare, you get *instadeath*. There are too many things in
Nethack in general that are insta-death-or-nothing. For instance,
"touch of death": if you don't have magic resistance, you die, if you
do then you take no damage. Or disintegration: if you have
disintegration resistance, no harm, if you do not then you die.

What Nethack really needs is things that can do *more hit point damage
without necessarily killing*. For instance, making such things as
fire, cold and shock resistances *reduce* damage by a percentage,
rather than doing no damage at all (this would also make Asmodeus a
worthy opponent, rather than somebody who continually hits you for no
damage until you finally do enough damage to take him down.) Or
reducing the amount of damage-reduction given by a high AC while
retaining the reduction in the chances of actually being hit, so that
if you do get hit you take a reasonable amount of actual damage.

So either you can be damaged more even when you have all the
resistances (thus making Gehennom a challenge rather than just a
cakewalk): or, else, you should suffer fewer instadeaths due to not
having specific resistances. Wands of death, touches of death and
items of instant stoning (aka cockatrice corpses), whether used by the
player or against him, are IMHO one of the things I dislike most about
Nethack.

